&lt;p&gt;All photos © Tyler Hughen.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Research Cruise Beaufort Sea 2015</title><link>https://gunnarvoet.net/post/research-cruise-arctic-2015/</link><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2015 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://gunnarvoet.net/post/research-cruise-arctic-2015/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Late August and September 2015 in the Beaufort Sea on R/V Sikuliaq to study how upper ocean turbulent mixing will change under ice-free conditions in a warmer climate. Increased turbulent mixing may bring up warmer Atlantic water from beneath the cold surface layer causing a positive feedback on Arctic sea ice retreat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We deployed a mooring in the central Beaufort Sea and carried out shipboard measurements with SWIMS and MMP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more info see our
&lt;a href="https://scripps.ucsd.edu/projects/arcticmix/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;cruise blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gunnarvoet.net/img/cruise-arctic-2015/sikuliaq.jpg" alt="r/v sikuliaq" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1181" height="656"&gt;
